# Module Development Guide

## Creating a New Module

### 1. Directory Structure
```bash
# Create module directories
mkdir -p Body/{role}/{ModuleName}/{Controllers,Models,Views}

# Example for public Blog module:
mkdir -p Body/public/Blog/{Controllers,Models,Views}
```

### 2. Controller (Body/{role}/{Module}/Controllers/module.php)
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

require_once ROOT . '/Brain/Core/Controller.php';

class BlogController extends Controller
{
    public function index(): void
    {
        // Load model using Loader
        $this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');
        
        // Get data
        $posts = $this->model_blog->getAllPosts();
        
        // Prepare view data
        $data = [
            'title' => 'Blog',
            'posts' => $posts
        ];
        
        // Load views
        $this->load->view('public/Common/header', $data);
        $this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);
        $this->load->view('public/Common/footer', $data);
    }
    
    public function show(): void
    {
        $id = $_GET['id'] ?? null;
        
        // Load model
        $this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');
        $post = $this->model_blog->getById((int)$id);
        
        // Load view
        $this->load->view('public/Blog/show', ['post' => $post]);
    }
}
```

### 3. Model (Body/{role}/{Module}/Models/{Module}Model.php)
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

require_once ROOT . '/Brain/Core/Model.php';

class BlogModel extends Model
{
    protected string $table = 'posts';
    
    public function getAllPosts(): array
    {
        $query = "SELECT * FROM {$this->table} ORDER BY created_at DESC";
        return $this->db->query($query)->fetchAll();
    }
    
    public function getById(int $id): ?array
    {
        $query = "SELECT * FROM {$this->table} WHERE id = ?";
        return $this->db->query($query, [$id])->fetch();
    }
    
    public function create(array $data): bool
    {
        $query = "INSERT INTO {$this->table} (title, content) VALUES (?, ?)";
        return $this->db->execute($query, [$data['title'], $data['content']]);
    }
}
```

### 4. View (Body/{role}/{Module}/Views/index.ct)
```php
<div class="module-page" style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px;">
    <h1><?= htmlspecialchars($title ?? 'Page') ?></h1>
    
    <?php if (!empty($posts)): ?>
        <?php foreach ($posts as $post): ?>
            <div class="post-card" style="border:1px solid #ddd;padding:15px;margin-bottom:10px;">
                <h2><?= htmlspecialchars($post['title']) ?></h2>
                <p><?= htmlspecialchars($post['content']) ?></p>
                <a href="<?= Router::url('blog.show', ['id' => $post['id']]) ?>">Read More</a>
            </div>
        <?php endforeach; ?>
    <?php else: ?>
        <p>No posts found.</p>
    <?php endif; ?>
</div>
```

### 5. Routes (Body/{role}/{Module}/routes.json)
```json
{
  "routes": [
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/blog",
      "handler": "public/Blog/Blog@index",
      "name": "blog.index"
    },
    {
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/blog/{id:\\d+}",
      "handler": "public/Blog/Blog@show",
      "name": "blog.show"
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/blog",
      "handler": "public/Blog/Blog@create",
      "name": "blog.create",
      "middleware": ["auth"]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Component Loading Patterns

### Load Model
```php
// Method 1: Using Loader
$this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');
$posts = $this->model_blog->getAllPosts();

// Method 2: Direct instantiation
$blogModel = new BlogModel($this->registry);
```

### Load Library
```php
$this->load->library('security/Validator');
$isValid = $this->validator->validate($data);
```

### Load Helper
```php
$this->load->helper('url');
// Helper functions now available
```

### Load View
```php
// Single view
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);

// Multiple views (typical pattern)
$this->load->view('public/Common/header', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Blog/index', $data);
$this->load->view('public/Common/footer', $data);
```

## Service Access

### Using Magic Accessors
```php
// Database
$users = $this->db->query("SELECT * FROM users")->fetchAll();

// Session
$userId = $this->session->get('user_id');
$this->session->set('key', 'value');

// Cache
$data = $this->cache->get('cache_key');
$this->cache->set('cache_key', $data, 3600);
```

## Route Parameters

### Define with Regex
```json
{
  "path": "/blog/{id:\\d+}",
  "path": "/user/{username:[a-z0-9_]+}",
  "path": "/post/{slug:[a-z0-9-]+}"
}
```

### Access in Controller
```php
public function show(): void
{
    $id = $_GET['id'] ?? null;
    $username = $_GET['username'] ?? null;
}
```

## Middleware

### Route-specific Middleware
```json
{
  "path": "/admin/dashboard",
  "handler": "admin/Dashboard@index",
  "middleware": ["auth", "admin"]
}
```

### Global Middleware
```php
// In Index/index.php or bootstrap
Router::middleware(['csrf', 'session']);
```

## Best Practices

1. **Always use strict typing**: `declare(strict_types=1);`
2. **Use named routes**: Always define `name` in routes.json
3. **Sanitize output**: Use `htmlspecialchars()` in views
4. **Type hint parameters**: `public function show(int $id): void`
5. **Load common views**: header/footer in most controllers
6. **Use Router for URLs**: `Router::url('route.name', $params)` instead of hardcoded paths
